there's a lot of battlefield 2042 news  today a new specialist map and mode have  been teased a massive patch just dropped  and big changes are happening at dice in  ea  following 2042's rocky launch ea has  announced a major shake-up at the  company dice general manager oscar  gabrielson is leaving with rebecca kutaz  set to take over as the new gm meanwhile  respawn co-founder vince sempela will  become the overall boss on the  battlefield franchise in addition to his  current role ea also indicated it's  looking to create a connected  battlefield universe and both ripple  effect and halo veteran marcus leto's  new studio will be working on  battlefield experiences which may or may  not be new games unfortunately many of  these future plans remain very vague for  the time being but you can read all  about everything we know on that at  gamespot.com  alongside the launch of today's major  new update for battlefield 2042 ea has  spoken a bit about what's next for the  game that includes the launch of a new  map and specialist which will hit next  year as well as time limited 64 player  modes for pc and new gen consoles  following the third update a new patch  is planned to arrive for battlefield  2042 later in december  but it's next year that we'll bring with  it a slate of new content including a  map called exposure while we didn't get  any specific details about its setting  or what it will involve ea tells  gamespot that it will be something  special by saying it takes map design to  a whole new level just what that means  is anyone's guess at this point 2022  will see the launch of the game's first  live season and will also be getting a  new specialist as well as weapons  gadgets and vehicles over the course of  the year we'll also get multiple seasons  each with its own set of new content  further specifics have not been shared  and we don't yet know the release  schedule for any of this  with the release of the new patch rush  mode can now be played on 2042's new  maps and weekly missions have been  reintroduced later in december ea will  add limited time matchmaking modes  allowing both conquest and breakthrough  to be played with just 64 players on pc  and ps5 xbox series x and s on these  platforms the modes are normally played  with 128 players one of the game's new  features with the launch of the new gen  hardware with the 64 player cap in place  for the last gen consoles ea also  reiterated its intent to continue  improving the core experience in the  wake of complaints about the game's  launch that will continue in the next  patch coming later this month and the  company said it's working to bring back  conspicuously absent fan favorite  systems such as a scoreboard it's also  working on unspecified improvements to  social systems  as far as today's patch goes for  battlefield 2042 well it's massive and  brings with it more than 150 bug fixes  changes and improvements across the game  as detailed by dice some of these  changes include improved level geometry  so that players don't get stuck the  elimination of various visual glitches  fixing the spawning issues and  adjustments to various collision issues  but that's just the tip of the iceberg  major changes are also coming to  battlefield 2042's ui the collection  screen is getting adjusted to make it  easier to use and clearer as to what  players are actually selecting new  indicators will soon show you which  players can revive you when you're  downed as well as indicators for players  that can provide health or ammo if you  are low on either enemy vehicles and  players will now also display health  bars when looked at from certain  distances  big additions are coming to the game's  battlefield portal mode as well  alongside various bug fixes for the mode  new builder options have been added such  as rush game modes for all of 2042's all  out warfare maps a new vehicle team  deathmatch mode and new official  templates for game types like gun master  and infection the update looks to also  fix a hit registration issue that has  been plaguing the game one that causes  bullets to deal no damage to enemy  targets dice says in the patch notes  that further improvements are still  being investigated in regards to this  issue battlefield 2042's launch has been  far from smooth early access players  frequently encountered server issues and  bugs while things have steadily improved  since then such as the thanksgiving day  update the buff weapon accuracy there is  still room for improvement dice is  currently planning at least one more  small patch for early december that will  bring more bug fixes as well as balance  changes you can read the full update  number three patch notes on gamespot.com  and be prepared because it's a lengthy  one  a lot of the time fixing one bug can  cause another according to a post from  the battlefield direct communication  twitter account some players on pc have  been unable to make horizontal mouse  inputs since downloading the patch  simply put it means they can't even look  both ways before crossing the street  naturally being unable to look left or  right in battlefield 2042 as it would in  any game is completely ruining the  experience for some players on pc that  being said there is a fix for the bug  but players will have to be willing to  lose all of their in-game settings to  implement it to re-enable horizontal  inputs on pc players will have to  navigate to my documents battlefield  2042 settings and then in their file  directory delete their prof save files  removing these files will restore the  game to his default settings which also  means losing any custom keybinds players  may have set however according to the  fan run twitter account battlefield  bulletin players only have to delete a  set number of lines in one file along  with that bug battlefield 2042  developers have noted an uptick in the  unable to low persistence data error  that prevents players from connecting to  a match  the error infamously stopped countless  users from getting into games after it  launched in early access this past  november unfortunately for players  there's nothing they can do to fix this  issue it's entirely server side so  they'll just have to wait for the game's  developers to address it  but wait there's even more battlefield  2042 news as the game might be adding  some seasonal themed skins according to  a leak including a santa costume for one  of the game's specialists which just  reminds me that we're somehow in  december already but okay if you've  hopped into battlefield how does the new  update feel any other new bugs popping  up anywhere let me know in the comments  and be sure to leave a like and  subscribe so you don't miss your next  episode of gamespot news  [Music]  you
 

